From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] dagu: wake the callback GMainContext after queue_callback

Against mutter 50.1 (Ubuntu libmutter-18 50.1-0ubuntu2.2).

meta_thread_queue_callback() only g_source_set_ready_time(source, 0).
GLib 2.88 skips the wakeup when ready_time is already 0, or when the
source is G_SOURCE_BLOCKED. The KMS thread path that pushes impl tasks
already calls g_main_context_wakeup(); the page-flip closure path does
not.

On dagu, after the first knife (do_handle_update never waits on the
Cogl sync_fd), dpu_crtc_complete_flip and flipped_in_impl land within
a few milliseconds of kickoff, but notify_view_crtc_presented often
arrives +75-229 ms later. The main thread is in ppoll. The next frame
is already in onscreen->next_frame; maybe_post cannot run until the
queued flip closure is dispatched.

Always wake the registered GMainContext after arming the source.

Live A/B on dagu (gnome-shell 128256, first knife still applied),
identity GTK lab, no Chrome:

  ELF 0x1d6ee4  bl set_ready_time  ->  bl cave
  cave: set_ready_time; g_main_context_wakeup(source->main_context)

---
 src/backends/native/meta-thread.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-thread.c b/src/backends/native/meta-thread.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-thread.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-thread.c
@@ -1179,6 +1179,7 @@ meta_thread_queue_callback (MetaThread         *thread,
   callback_source->callbacks = g_list_append (callback_source->callbacks,
                                               callback_data);
   g_source_set_ready_time (&callback_source->base, 0);
+  g_main_context_wakeup (main_context);
   g_mutex_unlock (&callback_source->mutex);
 }
 
 typedef struct _MetaSyncTaskData
